# TMX Language Conversion

A Python utility for modifying language codes in TMX (Translation Memory eXchange) files. Converts source language codes across the TMX header and all translation variant elements in a single pass – useful for localization engineers and PMs who need to realign translation memory files to a different locale variant.

**Repository:** [github.com/zirafinjezik/tmx-language-conversion](https://github.com/zirafinjezik/tmx-language-conversion)

---

## What It Does

- Replaces language codes in `xml:lang`, `srclang`, and `adminlang` attributes throughout the TMX file
- Handles SDL-generated TMX files (SDL Language Platform / Trados Studio format)
- Reads and writes UTF-8 encoded files, preserving all content and structure
- Outputs a new file without modifying the original

Default conversion: **en-US → en-GB**
The target pair is configurable by editing the `replacements` dictionary in the script.

---

## Use Cases

**Locale variant realignment**
A client switches their source locale from `en-US` to `en-GB` mid-project. All existing TMs need to be updated so that Trados Studio or memoQ can match against the correct source language. Running this script converts the entire TM file in seconds rather than manually editing XML.

**TM migration between regions**
A localization PM receives a TM from a US-based team and needs to integrate it into a UK-based workflow. The language code mismatch would prevent CAT tool matching – this script resolves it before import.

**Localization engineering pipeline**
A localization engineer building a file processing pipeline uses this script as a preprocessing step to normalise language codes before batch import into a TMS.

**QA validation example**
The included sample files (original and converted) demonstrate the before/after structure, making this repo useful as a reference for anyone learning TMX file manipulation or XML-aware string processing in Python.

---

## Why This Exists

CAT tools like Trados Studio and memoQ are strict about language code matching. A TM created with `en-US` as the source will not match against projects set to `en-GB`, even if the content is identical. Manually editing large TMX files in a text editor is error-prone and time-consuming. This script automates the conversion safely and repeatably.

---

